      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Think of an \"ingress gateway\" as a bouncer at a door who slows down the crowd slightly during busy times so nobody gets trampled or turned away angrily; a simple fix is to add a \"Try Again Later\" page when your site is too busy, which lets them wait instead of crashing. You can handle \"asynchronous processing\" by adding a simple background step that sends notifications only after the user has successfully created the food drive item, rather than trying to do everything instantly. This separates the user's main action from the notification step, ensuring your app never feels frozen because it's waiting to send an email or text.",
